            "accordion_row_GpGfEt": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How should I care for my leather piece?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "leather",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_xkKGPc": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Dust it with a soft, dry cloth; keep it out of prolonged sun, heat and damp; store it in its dust bag with a little tissue inside so it keeps its shape. Condition only when the leather feels dry, once or twice a year at most, with a cream made for fine smooth leather. If it gets wet, blot it and let it dry slowly, away from heat. The full guide, nubuck and exotic hides included, is on our <a href=\"/pages/leather-care-guide\">Leather Care</a> page.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "0.875rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
